🧰 Step 1 — Open Command Prompt in Project Folder
Go to your folder where all files are stored:
Example:

pc.v
instruction_memory.v
register_file.v
alu.v
control_unit.v
processor_top.v
tb_processor.v
Open CMD in that folder:

Shift + Right Click → Open Command Window Here
OR

cd Desktop\risc64
⚙️ Step 2 — Compile (Important Command)
Type:
Bash
iverilog -o risc_tb pc.v instruction_memory.v register_file.v alu.v control_unit.v processor_top.v tb_processor.v
If no error → compilation successful.
It will create a file:

risc_tb.vvp
▶️ Step 3 — Run Simulation
Bash
vvp risc_tb
After running, this file will be created:

processor.vcd
📊 Step 4 — Open Waveform
Bash
gtkwave processor.vcd
If GTKWave path not set, use full path:
Bash
"C:\Users\dhanr\Downloads\gtkwave-3.3.100-bin-win64\gtkwave64\bin\gtkwave.exe" processor.vcd
📈 Step 5 — Inside GTKWave
Add these signals:

clk
instruction
opcode
read_data1
read_data2
alu_op
alu_result
result
Then click Append → Insert → Zoom Fit.
